     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<br><br>I am a newbie to R and I am still learning my way around. I am currently\r\n attempting to plot multivariate data ( 18 rows and 96 columns with \r\nnumeric normalized data) using a Radar/Radial plot via ggplot. I have \r\nattached a image of the layout of my data to exemplify how my data \r\nlooks.<br><br><br><br><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-4O8jFmAFe2c/VbZTYQRId_I/AAAAAAAAABA/9aHopYqTbBw/s1600/table.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-4O8jFmAFe2c/VbZTYQRId_I/AAAAAAAAABA/9aHopYqTbBw/s1600/table.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368925056000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qeoWy2jhDTZzw28dfKkkz\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-4O8jFmAFe2c/VbZTYQRId_I/AAAAAAAAABA/9aHopYqTbBw/s400/table.jpg\" height=\"223\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"> I used the following modified code (highlighted in yellow) which I adapted from a similar yet simplified example and it doesn&#39;t seem to work. Any help or recommendations are welcome! Thank you in advance<br><br>Regards,<br>Raveen</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\">​</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">#Data framing<br>library(&quot;fmsb&quot;)<br>dd&lt;-data.frame(<br>  clust = 1:18,<br>  v1 &lt;- c(-0.10,-1.64,-0.85,-0.28,0.00,-1.34,-0.02,0.00,0.00,0.00,-0.15,-0.45,-1.07,-1.18,-0.18,0.17,-0.77,0.00),<br>  v2 &lt;- c(-0.41,-0.60,-1.14,-0.28,0.00,-1.34,-0.02,0.00,0.00,0.00,-0.15,-0.45,-1.07,-2.04,-0.12,-0.07,-0.77,-0.04),<br>  v3 &lt;- c(-